  Archon-o-phobes ascend at XL 14 or so.  The level of monsters
randomly generated depends half and half on XL and Dungeon Level,
until you do the invocation.  After that it depends on XL and the
level of Moloch's Sanctum.  (After you do the invocation is 
a poor time to try to gain 20 or so experience levels.)


  More XL gives higher max hp and max pwr.  And there are ways to
increase the amount that max hp and max pwr are increased.  (Yes,
increase the increase.)   

  It also gives more skill slots for #enhancement.  (Mostly 
important for ambitious wizards and those with mis-appropriated 
skill-slots.)

  For some spells, eg. magic missile and skilled+ cone of cold,
the amount of damage done per hit is [(XL/2) +1] d6, which is
roughly a little under twice the XL.

  XL 30 is a special case.  Once you hit XL 30 you can't raise
your XL any more, so there's no chance of getting tougher 
monsters.  You *can* keep gaining experience and getting the 
raises to max Hp and Pwr.

  So once you hit XL 30 you can keep getting tougher with no
risk of tougher monsters.


